    <DataNode elementId="Mannosyl5-N-acetyl-glucosamine2-R" textLabel="Man₅(GlcNAc)₃-[protein]" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="MNXM19209" dataSource="MetaNetX" />
      <Graphics centerX="350" centerY="400" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="kothari, SRI">According to the nomenclature used for hybrid and complex &lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-glycans, this compound is known as 2M&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;hy. The name is derived by having an &lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-acetylglucosaminyl residue added to a five mannose core (M5 core) by a &amp;beta;1-2 linkage. The term &quot;hy&quot; indicates that this is a hybrid &lt;I&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-glycan. Hybrid &lt;I&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-glycans are defined by having only mannosyl (Man) residues on the &amp;alpha;-Man-(1&amp;rarr;6) arm and only &lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-acetylglucosaminyl (GlcNAc) residues on the &amp;alpha;-Man-(1&amp;rarr;3) arm |CITS: [24178944]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="Mannosyl5-N-acetyl-glucosamine2-R" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Seed" value="cpd27493" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Metanetx" value="MNXM19209" />
